            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A guide wire includes a core shaft formed of superelastic metal, where the core shaft has a tapered portion having a diameter reducing from its own proximal end side toward the distal end side, an intermediate portion having an approximately cylindrical shape adjacent to the proximal end side of the tapered portion, and a proximal end portion adjacent to the proximal end side of the intermediate portion and having a diameter more increased than the intermediate portion; a coil body covering at least a part of the intermediate portion and the tapered portion of the core shaft, the coil body having an outer diameter of 0.36 mm or less; and a distal tip disposed at the distal end of the coil body and forming the distal end of the guide wire, the diameter of the intermediate portion being 0.22 mm or more to 0.24 mm or less.</p>
            </abstract>
